PJA 0.0.4 (tag v0.0.4, commit ceae7c7), https://github.com/YadeWira/PJA,
from the vendor tarball pja-0.0.4-zpaqstd.tar.gz (sha256
ccc43a309fc1446e9ec8545e61606cdd82a8ca40f44e6f791e4d50684039f92d), copied unmodified:
the sources of its zpaq-std plugin, LICENSE (MIT), NOTICE (IJG for the arithmetic-coded
JPEG, CharLS's BSD 3-Clause for JPEG-LS) and VENDOR.md (what it is and how it builds).

EXPERIMENTAL in zpaq-std, not recommended yet (-sa warns, 00737).
zpaq-std's codecs for specific formats, -sa: PJA's family, one plugin with three
codecs: pjax (JPEG that needs PJA's stream version 6: MPO and Ultra HDR, 12 bits, DNL,
DRI without RST), pja (JPEG) and pjals (JPEG-LS), stream version 5, full model. -sa and
-sa:pja use the three, in that order. Free Pascal: by the project's rule, a codec in
Rust or Free Pascal is built only as a plugin (codecs/pja.dll or pja.so, in the extra-codecs
download), never linked into zpaq-std itself. Every block carries the codec's ZPAQL
decoder (pas/plugin/pjazpaql.inc, pjalszpaql.inc, pjaxzpaql.inc), so any zpaq
extracts it without the plugin; those three programs are frozen under these codec names.
Do not patch these files here: send changes to the PJA repository.
